  "content": {
    "id": "p40-q20-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "20",
    "prompt": "A plane flies 1200 km on a NE compass bearing and then changes direction to a bearing of NW and flies for 450 km.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p40-q20-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "How far, correct to the nearest km, is the plane from its starting point?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "1282 km",
          "worked": "Let $S$ be the starting point, $T$ the turning point and $F$ the final position. Draw the two flight legs and a north arrow at $S$.\n\nThe bearing of $S$ from $T$ is $225^{\\circ}$, and the bearing of $F$ from $T$ is $315^{\\circ}$. Hence $\\angle STF=315^{\\circ}-225^{\\circ}=90^{\\circ}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}SF^2&=1200^2+450^2\\\\SF&=\\sqrt{1642500}\\\\SF&\\approx1282\\text{ km}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q20-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What is the bearing of the plane from its starting point, to the nearest minute?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$024^{\\circ}27'$",
          "worked": "Let $\\theta=\\angle TSF$. The final position lies to the north of the initial NE route, so subtract $\\theta$ from $045^{\\circ}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta&=\\frac{450}{1200}\\\\\\theta&=\\tan^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{450}{1200}\\right)\\\\\\text{Bearing of }F\\text{ from }S&=45^{\\circ}-\\tan^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{450}{1200}\\right)\\\\\\text{Bearing of }F\\text{ from }S&\\approx024^{\\circ}27'\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
  },
